{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sankeyDiagram"},{"type":"text","value":" lays out a directed weighted graph in final plot pixels, then\ncomposes ordinary marks over its nodes and links. Source rows stay semantic;\nthe application does not clone D3 records, resolve mutated endpoints, or\nmaterialize positioned DTOs."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart, link, rect, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sankeyDiagram } from '@tanstack/charts/network/sankey'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    sankeyDiagram({\n      nodes,\n      links,\n      nodeKey: 'id',\n      source: 'source',\n      target: 'target',\n      value: 'value',\n      align: 'left',\n      nodeWidth: ({ width }) => Math.max(12, width * 0.025),\n      nodePadding: ({ height }) => Math.max(12, height * 0.06),\n      inset: 24,\n      marks: ({ nodes: layoutNodes, links: layoutLinks }) =>\n        [\n          link(layoutLinks, {\n            x1: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y1',\n            x2: 'x2',\n            y2: 'y2',\n            key: 'key',\n            strokeWidth: (flow) => Math.max(1, flow.width),\n            lineCap: 'butt',\n          }),\n          rect(layoutNodes, {\n            x1: 'x0',\n            x2: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y0',\n            y2: 'y1',\n            key: 'key',\n            inset: 0,\n          }),\n          text(layoutNodes, {\n            x: 'x',\n            y: 'y',\n            text: (node) => node.data.label,\n            key: 'key',\n          }),\n        ] as const,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  guides: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/charts/network/sankey"},{"type":"text","value":" subpath keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3-sankey"},{"type":"text","value":" and the\nresolved flow adapter out of root, universal, force-layout, and ordinary-mark\nbundles. The Charts package owns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"d3-sankey"},{"type":"text","value":"; the application needs no direct\ndependency unless its own source imports that module."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"graph-input","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Graph input"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodes"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"links"},{"type":"text","value":" accept iterables. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeKey"},{"type":"text","value":" identifies each node; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":"\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"target"},{"type":"text","value":" read those keys from each link; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" reads its nonnegative\nweight."}]},{"type":"code","value":"sankeyDiagram({\n  nodes,\n  links,\n  nodeKey: 'id',\n  source: 'from',\n  target: 'to',\n  value: 'amount',\n  marks,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keys must be strings or finite numbers. Graph validation rejects duplicate\nnode keys, missing endpoints, duplicate authored link keys, and negative or\nnonfinite values. A nonempty graph must contain at least one positive link;\nzero-valued links may coexist with positive flow. The layout also rejects\ncycles."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linkKey"},{"type":"text","value":" when links can be reordered or when several links share the same\nendpoints. Without it, a unique raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" field is used when every link has one;\notherwise keys use source, target, and parallel-link occurrence."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input rows are never mutated. Accessors run when the mark is created; repeated\nresponsive layout passes use fresh private graph records."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Iterable<TNode>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic node rows"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"links"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Iterable<TLink>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic weighted edges"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TNode, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source-node identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"target"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Target-node identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TLink, number>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nonnegative link weight"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linkKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable link identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"align"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyAlignment | SankeyNodeAligner"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"justify"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in shorthand or D3-compatible node aligner"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeSort"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNodeComparator<TNode> | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"D3 order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same-column ordering; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" preserves input order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"linkSort"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLinkComparator<TNode, TLink> | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"D3 order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Link ordering inside each node; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" preserves input order"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeWidth"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | (chart: ChartBounds) => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"24"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Positive final-pixel node width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodePadding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | (chart: ChartBounds) => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nonnegative final-pixel separation within a layer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inset"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number | SankeyInset | responsive callback"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Final-pixel inset from the resolved plot bounds"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"iterations"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nonnegative integer relaxation-pass count"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marks"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(context: SankeyDiagramContext) => nonempty marks"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordinary marks over final-pixel node and link rows"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer-derived"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable parent mark identity"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"motion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartMotionDefinition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parent motion policy merged with each child's motion policy"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodeWidth"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nodePadding"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inset"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks receive the final\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartBounds"},{"type":"text","value":". Insets may be one number or separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"top"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"right"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bottom"},{"type":"text","value":",\nand "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"left"},{"type":"text","value":" values. The remaining extent must fit the node width and have a\npositive height."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"align"},{"type":"text","value":" also accepts a native D3 Sankey aligner or compatible callable:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { sankeyLeft } from 'd3-sankey'\n\nsankeyDiagram({\n  // graph channels and marks\n  align: sankeyLeft,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callable receives a private "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyAlignmentNode"},{"type":"text","value":" and the total column\ncount. Its raw node row is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node.data"},{"type":"text","value":"; D3 topology fields such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"depth"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceLinks"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"targetLinks"},{"type":"text","value":" are available on the same record.\nIt must synchronously return an integer from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":" through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnCount - 1"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe mark validates that result and creates fresh working records for every\nlayout pass, so do not retain or mutate them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"child-marks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Child marks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marks"},{"type":"text","value":" callback receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id, chart, nodes, links }"},{"type":"text","value":". It must return at\nleast one ordinary mark. Positional channels in those child marks are already\nfinal pixels, so a Sankey definition needs no x or y scale and normally hides\nCartesian guides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callback may run more than once while responsive margins and guides\nconverge. Keep it synchronous, deterministic, and free of input mutation or\nexternal side effects."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the callback for presentation that belongs to the visualization: link\ncurve and paint, node color, label side and wording, backdrops, or a title.\nThose decisions remain visible beside the marks rather than becoming hidden\nlayout data preparation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Child scene keys, mark IDs, and interaction points are scoped under the\nSankey mark. Color channels, layout labels, focus states, and child motion\nretain their ordinary behavior. A child cannot itself require resolved mark\nlayout; nested responsive layout passes are rejected."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"node-and-link-rows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node and link rows"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNode<TNode, TLink>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind: 'node'"},{"type":"text","value":", stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"index"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"depth"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"layer"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"aggregate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"final-pixel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":", and center "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"direct raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":" lineage; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"immutable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"incomingLinks"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outgoingLinks"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLink<TNode, TLink>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind: 'link'"},{"type":"text","value":", stable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":", raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceRows"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceIndexes"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceKey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"targetKey"},{"type":"text","value":", node indexes, and resolved "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sourceNode"},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"targetNode"},{"type":"text","value":";"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"semantic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":"; and"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"final-pixel "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y1"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x2"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y2"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The output rows and their lineage arrays are immutable. Node and link visual,\nsort, tooltip, and motion callbacks can reach the original row through\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact entry exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sankeyDiagram"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyAlignment"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyAlignmentNode"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNodeAligner"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyInset"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLayoutValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyEndpointContext"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNodeContext"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLinkContext"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNode"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLink"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyDiagramContext"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyNodeComparator"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyLinkComparator"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SankeyDiagramOptions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./rules-links-arrows-vectors-and-ticks.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rules, Links, Arrows, Vectors, and Ticks"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor link curves and paint, and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../examples/networks-and-hierarchies.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Networks and Hierarchies"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the\ncatalog cases."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"graph-input","text":"Graph input","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"child-marks","text":"Child marks","level":2},{"id":"node-and-link-rows","text":"Node and link rows","level":2},{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`sankeyDiagram` lays out a directed weighted graph in final plot pixels, then\ncomposes ordinary marks over its nodes and links. Source rows stay semantic;\nthe application does not clone D3 records, resolve mutated endpoints, or\nmaterialize positioned DTOs.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart, link, rect, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sankeyDiagram } from '@tanstack/charts/network/sankey'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    sankeyDiagram({\n      nodes,\n      links,\n      nodeKey: 'id',\n      source: 'source',\n      target: 'target',\n      value: 'value',\n      align: 'left',\n      nodeWidth: ({ width }) => Math.max(12, width * 0.025),\n      nodePadding: ({ height }) => Math.max(12, height * 0.06),\n      inset: 24,\n      marks: ({ nodes: layoutNodes, links: layoutLinks }) =>\n        [\n          link(layoutLinks, {\n            x1: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y1',\n            x2: 'x2',\n            y2: 'y2',\n            key: 'key',\n            strokeWidth: (flow) => Math.max(1, flow.width),\n            lineCap: 'butt',\n          }),\n          rect(layoutNodes, {\n            x1: 'x0',\n            x2: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y0',\n            y2: 'y1',\n            key: 'key',\n            inset: 0,\n          }),\n          text(layoutNodes, {\n            x: 'x',\n            y: 'y',\n            text: (node) => node.data.label,\n            key: 'key',\n          }),\n        ] as const,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  guides: false,\n})\n```\n\nThe exact `@tanstack/charts/network/sankey` subpath keeps `d3-sankey` and the\nresolved flow adapter out of root, universal, force-layout, and ordinary-mark\nbundles. The Charts package owns `d3-sankey`; the application needs no direct\ndependency unless its own source imports that module.\n\n## Graph input\n\n`nodes` and `links` accept iterables. `nodeKey` identifies each node; `source`\nand `target` read those keys from each link; `value` reads its nonnegative\nweight.\n\n```ts\nsankeyDiagram({\n  nodes,\n  links,\n  nodeKey: 'id',\n  source: 'from',\n  target: 'to',\n  value: 'amount',\n  marks,\n})\n```\n\nKeys must be strings or finite numbers. Graph validation rejects duplicate\nnode keys, missing endpoints, duplicate authored link keys, and negative or\nnonfinite values. A nonempty graph must contain at least one positive link;\nzero-valued links may coexist with positive flow. The layout also rejects\ncycles.\n\nUse `linkKey` when links can be reordered or when several links share the same\nendpoints. Without it, a unique raw `id` field is used when every link has one;\notherwise keys use source, target, and parallel-link occurrence.\n\nInput rows are never mutated. Accessors run when the mark is created; repeated\nresponsive layout passes use fresh private graph records.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                                | Default       | Meaning                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `nodes`       | `Iterable<TNode>`                                   | Required      | Semantic node rows                                           |\n| `links`       | `Iterable<TLink>`                                   | Required      | Semantic weighted edges                                      |\n| `nodeKey`     | `TransformValue<TNode, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Node identity                                                |\n| `source`      | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Source-node identity                                         |\n| `target`      | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Target-node identity                                         |\n| `value`       | `TransformValue<TLink, number>`                     | Required      | Nonnegative link weight                                      |\n| `linkKey`     | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Inferred      | Stable link identity                                         |\n| `align`       | `SankeyAlignment \\| SankeyNodeAligner`              | `justify`     | Built-in shorthand or D3-compatible node aligner             |\n| `nodeSort`    | `SankeyNodeComparator<TNode> \\| null`               | D3 order      | Same-column ordering; `null` preserves input order           |\n| `linkSort`    | `SankeyLinkComparator<TNode, TLink> \\| null`        | D3 order      | Link ordering inside each node; `null` preserves input order |\n| `nodeWidth`   | `number \\| (chart: ChartBounds) => number`          | `24`          | Positive final-pixel node width                              |\n| `nodePadding` | `number \\| (chart: ChartBounds) => number`          | `8`           | Nonnegative final-pixel separation within a layer            |\n| `inset`       | `number \\| SankeyInset \\| responsive callback`      | `0`           | Final-pixel inset from the resolved plot bounds              |\n| `iterations`  | `number`                                            | `6`           | Nonnegative integer relaxation-pass count                    |\n| `marks`       | `(context: SankeyDiagramContext) => nonempty marks` | Required      | Ordinary marks over final-pixel node and link rows           |\n| `id`          | `string`                                            | Layer-derived | Stable parent mark identity                                  |\n| `motion`      | `ChartMotionDefinition`                             | None          | Parent motion policy merged with each child's motion policy  |\n\nResponsive `nodeWidth`, `nodePadding`, and `inset` callbacks receive the final\n`ChartBounds`. Insets may be one number or separate `top`, `right`, `bottom`,\nand `left` values. The remaining extent must fit the node width and have a\npositive height.\n\n`align` also accepts a native D3 Sankey aligner or compatible callable:\n\n```ts\nimport { sankeyLeft } from 'd3-sankey'\n\nsankeyDiagram({\n  // graph channels and marks\n  align: sankeyLeft,\n})\n```\n\nThe callable receives a private `SankeyAlignmentNode` and the total column\ncount. Its raw node row is `node.data`; D3 topology fields such as `depth`,\n`height`, `sourceLinks`, and `targetLinks` are available on the same record.\nIt must synchronously return an integer from `0` through `columnCount - 1`.\nThe mark validates that result and creates fresh working records for every\nlayout pass, so do not retain or mutate them.\n\n## Child marks\n\nThe `marks` callback receives `{ id, chart, nodes, links }`. It must return at\nleast one ordinary mark. Positional channels in those child marks are already\nfinal pixels, so a Sankey definition needs no x or y scale and normally hides\nCartesian guides.\n\nThe callback may run more than once while responsive margins and guides\nconverge. Keep it synchronous, deterministic, and free of input mutation or\nexternal side effects.\n\nUse the callback for presentation that belongs to the visualization: link\ncurve and paint, node color, label side and wording, backdrops, or a title.\nThose decisions remain visible beside the marks rather than becoming hidden\nlayout data preparation.\n\nChild scene keys, mark IDs, and interaction points are scoped under the\nSankey mark. Color channels, layout labels, focus states, and child motion\nretain their ordinary behavior. A child cannot itself require resolved mark\nlayout; nested responsive layout passes are rejected.\n\n## Node and link rows\n\nEvery `SankeyNode<TNode, TLink>` contains:\n\n- `kind: 'node'`, stable `key`, `index`, `depth`, `height`, and `layer`;\n- aggregate `value`;\n- final-pixel `x0`, `x1`, `y0`, `y1`, and center `x`, `y`;\n- direct raw `data`, `source`, and `sourceIndexes` lineage; and\n- immutable `incomingLinks` and `outgoingLinks`.\n\nEvery `SankeyLink<TNode, TLink>` contains:\n\n- `kind: 'link'`, stable `key`, raw `data`, `sourceRows`, and\n  `sourceIndexes`;\n- `sourceKey`, `targetKey`, node indexes, and resolved `sourceNode` and\n  `targetNode`;\n- semantic `value`; and\n- final-pixel `width`, `x1`, `y1`, `x2`, and `y2`.\n\nThe output rows and their lineage arrays are immutable. Node and link visual,\nsort, tooltip, and motion callbacks can reach the original row through\n`data`.\n\n## Types\n\nThe exact entry exports `sankeyDiagram`, `SankeyAlignment`,\n`SankeyAlignmentNode`, `SankeyNodeAligner`, `SankeyInset`,\n`SankeyLayoutValue`, `SankeyEndpointContext`, `SankeyNodeContext`,\n`SankeyLinkContext`, `SankeyNode`, `SankeyLink`, `SankeyDiagramContext`,\n`SankeyNodeComparator`, `SankeyLinkComparator`, and `SankeyDiagramOptions`.\n\nSee [Rules, Links, Arrows, Vectors, and Ticks](./rules-links-arrows-vectors-and-ticks.md)\nfor link curves and paint, and\n[Networks and Hierarchies](../../examples/networks-and-hierarchies.md) for the\ncatalog cases.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sankey Diagram Mark\ndescription: Reference for responsive flow layout, semantic graph input, immutable node and link rows, ordinary child marks, and the optional Sankey import.\n---\n\n`sankeyDiagram` lays out a directed weighted graph in final plot pixels, then\ncomposes ordinary marks over its nodes and links. Source rows stay semantic;\nthe application does not clone D3 records, resolve mutated endpoints, or\nmaterialize positioned DTOs.\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart, link, rect, text } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { sankeyDiagram } from '@tanstack/charts/network/sankey'\n\nconst chart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    sankeyDiagram({\n      nodes,\n      links,\n      nodeKey: 'id',\n      source: 'source',\n      target: 'target',\n      value: 'value',\n      align: 'left',\n      nodeWidth: ({ width }) => Math.max(12, width * 0.025),\n      nodePadding: ({ height }) => Math.max(12, height * 0.06),\n      inset: 24,\n      marks: ({ nodes: layoutNodes, links: layoutLinks }) =>\n        [\n          link(layoutLinks, {\n            x1: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y1',\n            x2: 'x2',\n            y2: 'y2',\n            key: 'key',\n            strokeWidth: (flow) => Math.max(1, flow.width),\n            lineCap: 'butt',\n          }),\n          rect(layoutNodes, {\n            x1: 'x0',\n            x2: 'x1',\n            y1: 'y0',\n            y2: 'y1',\n            key: 'key',\n            inset: 0,\n          }),\n          text(layoutNodes, {\n            x: 'x',\n            y: 'y',\n            text: (node) => node.data.label,\n            key: 'key',\n          }),\n        ] as const,\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: null,\n    y: null,\n  },\n  guides: false,\n})\n```\n\nThe exact `@tanstack/charts/network/sankey` subpath keeps `d3-sankey` and the\nresolved flow adapter out of root, universal, force-layout, and ordinary-mark\nbundles. The Charts package owns `d3-sankey`; the application needs no direct\ndependency unless its own source imports that module.\n\n## Graph input\n\n`nodes` and `links` accept iterables. `nodeKey` identifies each node; `source`\nand `target` read those keys from each link; `value` reads its nonnegative\nweight.\n\n```ts\nsankeyDiagram({\n  nodes,\n  links,\n  nodeKey: 'id',\n  source: 'from',\n  target: 'to',\n  value: 'amount',\n  marks,\n})\n```\n\nKeys must be strings or finite numbers. Graph validation rejects duplicate\nnode keys, missing endpoints, duplicate authored link keys, and negative or\nnonfinite values. A nonempty graph must contain at least one positive link;\nzero-valued links may coexist with positive flow. The layout also rejects\ncycles.\n\nUse `linkKey` when links can be reordered or when several links share the same\nendpoints. Without it, a unique raw `id` field is used when every link has one;\notherwise keys use source, target, and parallel-link occurrence.\n\nInput rows are never mutated. Accessors run when the mark is created; repeated\nresponsive layout passes use fresh private graph records.\n\n## Options\n\n| Option        | Type                                                | Default       | Meaning                                                      |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `nodes`       | `Iterable<TNode>`                                   | Required      | Semantic node rows                                           |\n| `links`       | `Iterable<TLink>`                                   | Required      | Semantic weighted edges                                      |\n| `nodeKey`     | `TransformValue<TNode, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Node identity                                                |\n| `source`      | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Source-node identity                                         |\n| `target`      | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Required      | Target-node identity                                         |\n| `value`       | `TransformValue<TLink, number>`                     | Required      | Nonnegative link weight                                      |\n| `linkKey`     | `TransformValue<TLink, ChartKey>`                   | Inferred      | Stable link identity                                         |\n| `align`       | `SankeyAlignment \\| SankeyNodeAligner`              | `justify`     | Built-in shorthand or D3-compatible node aligner             |\n| `nodeSort`    | `SankeyNodeComparator<TNode> \\| null`               | D3 order      | Same-column ordering; `null` preserves input order           |\n| `linkSort`    | `SankeyLinkComparator<TNode, TLink> \\| null`        | D3 order      | Link ordering inside each node; `null` preserves input order |\n| `nodeWidth`   | `number \\| (chart: ChartBounds) => number`          | `24`          | Positive final-pixel node width                              |\n| `nodePadding` | `number \\| (chart: ChartBounds) => number`          | `8`           | Nonnegative final-pixel separation within a layer            |\n| `inset`       | `number \\| SankeyInset \\| responsive callback`      | `0`           | Final-pixel inset from the resolved plot bounds              |\n| `iterations`  | `number`                                            | `6`           | Nonnegative integer relaxation-pass count                    |\n| `marks`       | `(context: SankeyDiagramContext) => nonempty marks` | Required      | Ordinary marks over final-pixel node and link rows           |\n| `id`          | `string`                                            | Layer-derived | Stable parent mark identity                                  |\n| `motion`      | `ChartMotionDefinition`                             | None          | Parent motion policy merged with each child's motion policy  |\n\nResponsive `nodeWidth`, `nodePadding`, and `inset` callbacks receive the final\n`ChartBounds`. Insets may be one number or separate `top`, `right`, `bottom`,\nand `left` values. The remaining extent must fit the node width and have a\npositive height.\n\n`align` also accepts a native D3 Sankey aligner or compatible callable:\n\n```ts\nimport { sankeyLeft } from 'd3-sankey'\n\nsankeyDiagram({\n  // graph channels and marks\n  align: sankeyLeft,\n})\n```\n\nThe callable receives a private `SankeyAlignmentNode` and the total column\ncount. Its raw node row is `node.data`; D3 topology fields such as `depth`,\n`height`, `sourceLinks`, and `targetLinks` are available on the same record.\nIt must synchronously return an integer from `0` through `columnCount - 1`.\nThe mark validates that result and creates fresh working records for every\nlayout pass, so do not retain or mutate them.\n\n## Child marks\n\nThe `marks` callback receives `{ id, chart, nodes, links }`. It must return at\nleast one ordinary mark. Positional channels in those child marks are already\nfinal pixels, so a Sankey definition needs no x or y scale and normally hides\nCartesian guides.\n\nThe callback may run more than once while responsive margins and guides\nconverge. Keep it synchronous, deterministic, and free of input mutation or\nexternal side effects.\n\nUse the callback for presentation that belongs to the visualization: link\ncurve and paint, node color, label side and wording, backdrops, or a title.\nThose decisions remain visible beside the marks rather than becoming hidden\nlayout data preparation.\n\nChild scene keys, mark IDs, and interaction points are scoped under the\nSankey mark. Color channels, layout labels, focus states, and child motion\nretain their ordinary behavior. A child cannot itself require resolved mark\nlayout; nested responsive layout passes are rejected.\n\n## Node and link rows\n\nEvery `SankeyNode<TNode, TLink>` contains:\n\n- `kind: 'node'`, stable `key`, `index`, `depth`, `height`, and `layer`;\n- aggregate `value`;\n- final-pixel `x0`, `x1`, `y0`, `y1`, and center `x`, `y`;\n- direct raw `data`, `source`, and `sourceIndexes` lineage; and\n- immutable `incomingLinks` and `outgoingLinks`.\n\nEvery `SankeyLink<TNode, TLink>` contains:\n\n- `kind: 'link'`, stable `key`, raw `data`, `sourceRows`, and\n  `sourceIndexes`;\n- `sourceKey`, `targetKey`, node indexes, and resolved `sourceNode` and\n  `targetNode`;\n- semantic `value`; and\n- final-pixel `width`, `x1`, `y1`, `x2`, and `y2`.\n\nThe output rows and their lineage arrays are immutable. Node and link visual,\nsort, tooltip, and motion callbacks can reach the original row through\n`data`.\n\n## Types\n\nThe exact entry exports `sankeyDiagram`, `SankeyAlignment`,\n`SankeyAlignmentNode`, `SankeyNodeAligner`, `SankeyInset`,\n`SankeyLayoutValue`, `SankeyEndpointContext`, `SankeyNodeContext`,\n`SankeyLinkContext`, `SankeyNode`, `SankeyLink`, `SankeyDiagramContext`,\n`SankeyNodeComparator`, `SankeyLinkComparator`, and `SankeyDiagramOptions`.\n\nSee [Rules, Links, Arrows, Vectors, and Ticks](./rules-links-arrows-vectors-and-ticks.md)\nfor link curves and paint, and\n[Networks and Hierarchies](../../examples/networks-and-hierarchies.md) for the\ncatalog cases.\n"}
